#######################################################################################
# NETWORK ACCESS CONTROL
# =======================
# By default, ALL network connections are denied. Use explicit rules to allow access.
#
# Rule format: net=<ACTION>|<PROTOCOL>|<NETWORK>|<PORTS>|<DIRECTION>
# - ACTION: ALLOW or DENY
# - PROTOCOL: tcp, udp, or * (any)
# - NETWORK: IP/CIDR, hostname, or * (any)
# - PORTS: port number, range (80-443), list (80,443), or * (any)
# - DIRECTION: IN (server), OUT (client), or * (both)
#
# Security guidelines:
# - Use most restrictive rules possible
# - Prefer specific ports over wildcards
# - Consider blocking internal networks to prevent lateral movement
# - Review rules regularly and remove unused access
#
# If you use a hostname in a rule, read 'wiki/dns.md' to fully understand the limitations of this approach.

# Common outbound web access:
#net=ALLOW|tcp|0.0.0.0/0|443|OUT         # HTTPS to anywhere
#net=ALLOW|tcp|0.0.0.0/0|80|OUT          # HTTP to anywhere

# Local server binding:
#net=ALLOW|tcp|0.0.0.0/0|${PORT:-8000}|IN    # Accept connections on port

# Block internal networks (recommended for production):
#net=DENY|*|10.0.0.0/8|*|OUT             # Private Class A
#net=DENY|*|172.16.0.0/12|*|OUT          # Private Class B
#net=DENY|*|192.168.0.0/16|*|OUT         # Private Class C
#net=DENY|*|169.254.0.0/16|*|OUT         # Link-local
#net=DENY|*|127.0.0.0/8|*|OUT            # Loopback
#net=DENY|*|fc00::/7|*|OUT               # IPv6 ULA
#net=DENY|*|fe80::/10|*|OUT              # IPv6 Link-local
# TODO: /etc/firejail/nolocal.net

# Generated rules from learning mode:
